In July 2012, Osborn made it through stringent requirements for a clinical trial at St. Joseph Hospital of Orange and received a renal artery denervation, becoming the first person in Southern California to undergo the procedure.
The clinical trial focused on patients with resistant high blood pressure, meaning they were taking at least three medications but were still unable to control their blood pressure.
